<title>FRANCE: GAN rises on CIC tender report.</title>
<headline>GAN rises on CIC tender report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer GAN was up 3.52 percent on speculation in a Paris business daily that the tender for the partial privatisation of its banking arm CIC might be relaunched, traders said.</p>
<p>The newspaper AGEFI said the tender might be withdrawn because the terms and conditions attached to CIC's sale were proving too onerous and that the price fetched as a result would be too low.</p>
<p>It speculated that government may instead choose to relaunch the tender, and decide to sell off GAN and CIC together which, it said, would preserve the synergies of the two groups.</p>
<p>CIC was off 4.76 percent.</p>
<p>The newspaper said that only French banks Societe Generale and BNP remained in the running for CIC.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
